Description: Incident-first root-cause analysis console for Linux
 v0.49.0 — Security hardening, memory/concurrency fixes, test + CI
 infrastructure. Groundwork for Phase 2 journal-driven service RCA and
 Phase 4 config-drift detection.
 .
 This release solidifies the Phase 1 proof-system architecture with:
 .
   Security & Stability
     * buffer overflow fix in SMART parser
     * race condition fixes in host tracking (fleet hub)
     * proper resource cleanup in engine shutdown
     * unbounded cache eviction in kubepods tracking
 .
   Test Infrastructure
     * test coverage improvements
     * integration test harness for RCA replay
 .
   Groundwork for Phase 2 & Phase 4
     * journal entry types and structured JSON parsing
     * config snapshot collector framework
     * ready for service RCA via systemd journal findings
     * ready for config-drift detection vs baseline
 .
 All v0.48.0 features (NEXTGEN proof-system, multi-gate verifier,
 entity graph, replay corpus) remain intact and unchanged.
